{"name":"Devilish Diva","hex":"#ce7790","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"devilish","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Resembling a devil.","Evil, wicked."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Devilishly; very; exceedingly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/devilish"},{"term":"diva","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any female celebrity, usually a well known singer or actress. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person with an inflated sense of self, who has high expectations of others, and who is extremely demanding and fussy when it comes to personal privileges."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diva"}],"entries":[{"title":"Devil","blocks":[{"text":"The devil is a mythical personification of evil as conceived in various cultures and religious traditions. It is seen as the objectification of a hostile and destructive force. Jeffrey Burton Russell states that the different conceptions of the Devil can be summed up as 1. a principle of evil independent from God, 2. an aspect of God, 3. a created being turning evil or 4. a symbol of human evil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/022_devil_representation.JPG/330px-022_devil_representation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil"},{"title":"Diva","blocks":[{"text":"Diva, the Latin word for a goddess, has often been used as an honorific to refer to a celebrated woman of outstanding talent in the world of opera, theatre, cinema, fashion and popular music. If referring to an actress, the meaning of diva is closely related to that of prima donna. Diva can also refer to a person, especially one in show business, with a reputation for being temperamental or demanding. The application of the term has broadened beyond the performing arts to also include celebrated political and business figures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Mariah_Carey_-_Beautiful_%28Live_%40_GMA%2C_May_24%2C_2013%29.JPG/330px-Mariah_Carey_-_Beautiful_%28Live_%40_GMA%2C_May_24%2C_2013%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diva"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/120px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/250px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/120px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Excerpt of a Byzantine-Mosaic-Image. A blue angel, probably representing the Devil, standing before goats. Early 6th century.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlueAngel.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg/500px-Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg/1280px-Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg/500px-Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Devil on horseback. Nuremberg Chronicle (1493).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Wo